UID:0d6a3607f0397fa6@role-professional-responsibility.maine-government-fee
 ds
DTSTAMP:20260810T191354Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260803
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Standing Order: Standing Order on Servicememb
 ers or Spouses of Servicemembers Seeking Admission to the Maine Bar
DESCRIPTION:STATE OF MAINE \nSUPREME JUDICIAL COURT \nSTANDING ORDER ON SE
 RVICEMEMBERS OR SPOUSES OF SERVICEMEMBERS \nSEEKING ADMISSION TO THE MAINE
  BAR \n \nEffective August 3\, 2026 \nAttorneys who are servicemembers or 
 spouses of servicemembers \nassigned to Maine and who wish to be licensed 
 in Maine while they or their \nspouses are stationed here may seek waiver 
 of strict compliance with the \nduration of practice requirement of the ru
 le g overning admission by motion \nwithout examination\, Maine Bar Admiss
 ion Rule 11A(a)(2).  The Maine \nSupreme Judicial Court\, the Maine Board 
 of Overseers of the Bar\, and the Maine \nBoard of Bar Examiners are commi
 tted to working with these applicants to \naccommodate their unique circum
 stances and to expedite the bar application \nprocess to the extent possib
 le when they or their spouses’ service brings them \nto Maine. \nThe Cou
 rt will consider requests for waiver on a case -by-case basis\, \ndependin
 g on the individual circumstances of the applicant.   Servicemembers \nand
  spouses of servicemembers are encouraged to contact the Maine Supreme \nJ
 udicial Court Clerk’s Office at (207)822-4146 for more information about
  the \nwaiver process. Servicemembers and spouses of servicemembers assign
 ed to \nMaine who wish to take the Maine bar examination but have missed a
  deadline \nto apply for the exam\, should also contact the Maine Board of
  Bar Examiners at \n(207)623-2464 or execdir@mainebarexaminers.org for ass
 istance. \nPromulgation Date: 8/3/2026 FOR THE COURT: \n \n \n   /s/      
 \nVALERIE STANFILL \nChief Justice \n \nAndrew M. Mead \nCatherine R. Conn
 ors \nRick E. Lawrence \nWayne R. Douglas \nJulia M. Lipez \nChristopher C
 . Taub\nhttps://www.courts.maine.gov/adminorders/so-service-members.pdf
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/adminorders/so-service-members.pdf
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
